## Cohort Delivery Layer (Class)

Delivery defines **when / with whom** students learn. Separate from curriculum content.

```
Program
└── Class                            (đợt học — cohort instance)
    ├── ClassEnrollment              (student ↔ cohort, linked to ProgramEnrollment)
    └── ClassSession                 (calendar event for this cohort)
            ├── Activity?            (lesson / lab / field trip)
            └── Assignment?          (assignment window)
                    └── SessionAttendance
```

| Entity | Role |
|--------|------|
| **Class** | Running cohort: mentor, start/end dates, capacity, schedule summary, late-join guard |
| **ClassEnrollment** | Links student to cohort; one active class per program enrollment (v1) |
| **ClassSession** | Scheduled event (`SessionKind`: Lesson, LiveOnline, FieldTrip, AssignmentWindow, MentorCheckIn) |
| **SessionAttendance** | Roster attendance per session, tied to `ModuleEnrollment` |
| **ActivityBooking** | Student slot booking for Live/Offline activities (unique per student + activity) |

**Scheduling split:**
- `Activity.StartTime` / `EndTime` / `Location` = **template defaults** on the content blueprint
- `ClassSession.StartTime` / `EndTime` / `Location` = **actual cohort schedule**
- `Activity.SchedulingMode`: SelfPaced, ClassSynchronized, OptionalBooking
- `Module.DefaultSchedulingMode` — suggested default for new activities

**Mentor assignment (MVP direction):**
- Prefer **`Class.MentorId`** for the instructor of a running cohort
- `Course.MentorId` is legacy/content-author field — do not use for cohort scheduling

